Still 1.2.0. The tap gesture, with the threshold measured instead of guessed.

Your two recordings settled it: the taps were never faint — every audible one reached 22 to 60 dB over the noise floor. The margin was simply far too low, so most of a hand-held recording counted as a tap and the detector was always mid-count when a real one arrived.

12 dB became 30, and the pulse and gap windows widened to match. Zero false arms on that corpus.

Expect to repeat a gesture now and then.
